    "leafs": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Maple Leafs",
      "league": "NHL",
      "record": "32-36-14",
      "detail": "8th in Atlantic Division",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The season ended the way too many Maple Leafs seasons do - with a stack of questions and not nearly enough answers. <strong>Toronto's 32-36-14 finish, good for 78 points and 8th in the Atlantic Division, left it 15th overall and staring at another summer of reckoning</strong>; the streak ran to seven losses, and that is the kind of flatline that turns patience into pressure. The core talent was never the issue. The Leafs had enough skill to flash, but not enough backbone to sustain it, and that is the indictment hanging over the room now. Mitch Marner is still a headline name, and the broader conversation around the roster will center on whether the club can keep its big pieces, clear dead weight, and find a coach or system that stops the same old collapse from repeating. Management has decisions to make on free agency, the draft, and whether the current blueprint deserves one more chance. <strong>What happens next - coaching, contracts, and whether the Leafs finally choose a real reset - will define this franchise's summer</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated June 8, 2026"
      },
