    "jays": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Blue Jays",
      "league": "MLB",
      "record": "32-34",
      "detail": "3rd in AL East",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The season has settled into a hard-edged little fight now - and the Blue Jays are at least throwing their punches. <strong>Toronto beat Baltimore 6-4 last night for its second straight win, taking the final two games of the series</strong>, a tidy answer after getting thumped 13-3 on Friday and a reminder that this club still has some backbone. At 32-34, third in the AL East and seven games back, the Jays are not charging the division so much as chasing respectability, but a 2-0 surge is better than the alternative and keeps them hanging around the wild-card fringe with a 7th seed. The formula has been simple enough: enough offense to survive, enough outs to close the door. The bullpen did that in the end, and Ernie Clement's sharp work at the plate and in the field in the series finale stood out in the highlight reel. <strong>Now comes a far stiffer test tonight against the Phillies at 6:07 p.m. ET, and Toronto has to prove the Baltimore bounce was a turn, not a pause</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated June 8, 2026"
      },
