        "body": "Camp is where the truth starts leaking out, and right now the Commanders are living in the awkward, necessary middle of the job - sorting the roster, teaching the new pieces, and finding out who can handle the heat when the pads finally come on. <strong>The most important development is the opening of OTAs and minicamp, where the real competition now begins in earnest</strong>. Washington sits 3rd in the NFC East, with a W1 streak, 6 games behind, and a playoff seed of 14, but those numbers are just the frame; the picture will be painted by how quickly the new arrivals absorb the scheme and how the draft class survives the first serious test of NFL speed. This is the season of first impressions - the quarterback room, the secondary, the edge rotation, all of it. Somebody is going to grab this thing and make the coaches stop asking questions. Others will disappear into the pile. <strong>What to watch next: which young player turns a clean spring into a real roster claim before training camp hardens the depth chart</strong>.",
